# Settings for vision.mycomap.org. provision.sh copies this to
# /etc/mycomap-vision/vision.env (mode 600) and links <repo>/.env to it, so the
# service and the `mv` command read the same values. Fill in the <...> values.
# No secrets go in here: the session secret, the sign-in public key and the AWS
# key live in their own files.

# Where releases are pulled to; the server serves the one current.txt names.
MV_RELEASE_ROOT=/srv/mycomap-vision

# The private bucket and its region (the same as on the laptop's .env).
MV_S3_BUCKET=<BUCKET>
MV_AWS_REGION=<REGION>
# The box's AWS profile a person entered with `aws configure --profile ...`: it reads
# releases/ and keeps the site's run links under site-runs/ (box-policy.template.json).
MV_AWS_PROFILE=mycomap-vision-box
# Every identification on the site kept under its own link /r/<id> (runs.py), in the
# bucket's site-runs/; its owner index in <release root>/state/site-runs.sqlite.
MV_RUN_LINKS=s3
# The Identify page's "Example result": one kept run's id (the 16 characters after /r/),
# set on the box only. Unset: the page shows no example.
# MV_EXAMPLE_RUN=

# Sign-in with a mycomap.org account: all = the whole site (pre-launch),
# identify = only identifications, off = open.
MV_SIGNIN=all
MV_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://vision.mycomap.org
MV_SIGNIN_ISSUER=https://mycomap.org
MV_SIGNIN_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE=/etc/mycomap-vision/signin-public.pem
MV_SESSION_SECRET_FILE=/etc/mycomap-vision/session-secret

# Photographers' answers from mycomap.org (permissions.py), re-read every 5 minutes.
# The key is the value set as VISION_API_KEY on mycomap.org, in its own file
# (mode 600, owner ubuntu). Without it, all-rights-reserved photos are never shown.
MV_ORG_BASE_URL=https://mycomap.org
MV_ORG_VISION_KEY_FILE=/etc/mycomap-vision/org-vision-key
# Re-read photo licences from iNat daily (~800 requests at 1/s).
MV_LICENSE_REFRESH_HOURS=24

# The nightly update (nightly.py, docs/deploy.md "Nightly update"): new, removed and
# renamed green records from mycomap.org every night at 3 a.m. Eastern, with the key
# above. Off until mycomap.org serves /api/vision/green-records and Cloudflare lets
# this box through to /api/vision/; check first with `mv nightly --plan`.
# MV_NIGHTLY=1

# What the public API may run. One model (sized for a 4 GB box; the live box is
# 16 GB / 4 vCPU as of 2026-10-25), and only the method that
# answers in seconds; the box never trains a classifier itself (minutes of CPU now,
# hours at the full photo set): trained methods come ready-made in a release.
MV_ALLOWED_BACKBONES=bioclip-2
MV_METHODS=nearest,nearest+mean
# The method used when none is named (Steve 2026-10-09: nearest + species average). It must
# be in MV_METHODS, and its calibration must be on this box's scoreboard (import the
# comparison's rows with mv scoreboard-import) before it is switched on.
MV_DEFAULT_METHOD=nearest+mean
# Place and date (Steve 2026-10-11; placeprior.py): nearest+mean+place adds the boost prior
# when an identification has a place or date, and is nearest+mean exactly otherwise (it
# uses nearest+mean's calibration). It needs a release that carries
# occurrence/inat-fungi-na.npz (mv release ships it when built); without that file it is
# not offered and the default falls back to nearest+mean. About 35 MB more resident on this
# box, ~80 ms per identification with a place. To switch it on, both lines:
#   MV_METHODS=nearest,nearest+mean,nearest+mean+place
#   MV_DEFAULT_METHOD=nearest+mean+place
# Scoring by specimen (Steve 2026-10-18, E32): nearest+mean-records-balanced(+place) takes a
# species' two best SPECIMENS (records, an MO/iNat cross-post of one find counted once) and
# a species average in which each specimen counts once. It needs the cross-post twin groups:
# twin-groups.tsv in the release (mv release --twin-groups FILE) or MV_TWIN_GROUPS; without them it is not
# offered, and the default falls back: (c)+place -> (c) -> nearest+mean+place -> nearest+mean.
# Its calibration rows must be on the scoreboard first. To switch it on, both lines:
#   MV_METHODS=nearest,nearest+mean,nearest+mean+place,nearest+mean-records-balanced,nearest+mean-records-balanced+place
#   MV_DEFAULT_METHOD=nearest+mean-records-balanced+place
# Roll back: MV_DEFAULT_METHOD=nearest+mean+place.
# MV_TWIN_GROUPS=
MV_FIT_ON_DEMAND=0
# At most this many models per identification (side-by-side comparison).
MV_MAX_MODELS=2
# Load it (and its index) at startup, not on the first identification.
MV_PRELOAD=default
MV_RATE_LIMIT=30/600
MV_MAX_QUEUE=2

# Model weights cache (filled by provision.sh) and CPU threads: the box's vCPU count
# (2 on the 4 GB plan this template was written for; 4 on the 16 GB box).
HF_HOME=/srv/mycomap-vision/hf
HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
OMP_NUM_THREADS=2
